33
00:02:45.272 --> 00:02:53.501
For each type of puzzle, students will develop
and implement both optimal solving algorithms

34
00:02:53.501 --> 00:02:57.616
and algorithms that mimic human solving
processes.

35
00:02:57.616 --> 00:03:03.112
Consider this worked case: A traveling
salesman puzzle uses nearest-neighbor

36
00:03:03.112 --> 00:03:10.256
heuristics to quickly generate a route, even
if it is not mathematically optimal.

37
00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:17.501
Compare alternatives against the same
constraints so the evaluation does not move

38
00:03:17.501 --> 00:03:18.709
