51
00:04:17.304 --> 00:04:24.101
Graphs can be represented with adjacency
structures for traversal and path algorithms.

52
00:04:24.101 --> 00:04:30.758
Consider this worked case: A stack stores the
sequence of moves in a maze solver, allowing

53
00:04:30.758 --> 00:04:35.335
the program to reverse steps when a dead end
is reached.

54
00:04:35.335 --> 00:04:41.945
State the benefit, the cost, and the condition
under which the tradeoff is acceptable.

55
00:04:41.945 --> 00:04:49.491
Making the tradeoff visible prevents a local
improvement from hiding a larger cost.

56
00:04:49.610 --> 00:04:55.571
Stress-test the reasoning around
Human-Inspired vs. Optimal Approaches with an

57
00:04:55.571 --> 00:05:00.935
